WEBVTT

00:06.400 --> 00:11.040
♪ Take a little walk
To the edge of town ♪

00:11.160 --> 00:13.640
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

00:16.520 --> 00:19.080
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

00:19.160 --> 00:21.840
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

00:21.960 --> 00:25.920
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

00:27.480 --> 00:32.520
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

00:32.600 --> 00:35.000
♪ In the humming wires ♪

00:35.080 --> 00:36.360
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

00:36.480 --> 00:39.040
♪ You're never coming back ♪

00:39.160 --> 00:42.000
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

00:43.160 --> 00:44.520
Shoot out his tires...

00:46.160 --> 00:47.000
[in Italian]

00:47.080 --> 00:48.080
He may try to surrender.

00:48.200 --> 00:49.120
[in English] But remember...

00:51.040 --> 00:52.680
I'll fire the final shot.

00:52.800 --> 00:54.600
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

00:54.720 --> 00:56.920
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

00:57.000 --> 01:00.240
♪ A red right hand ♪

01:39.600 --> 01:40.720
Stay inside, ma'am.

01:52.440 --> 01:54.240
[gunfire]

02:09.400 --> 02:10.240
Come on!

02:24.000 --> 02:24.880
Go, go, go!

02:26.800 --> 02:28.160
[in Italian]

02:28.280 --> 02:29.800
He was prepared.

02:30.920 --> 02:32.560
Don't let him get away!

02:35.720 --> 02:37.400
That bitch lied to me.

02:39.760 --> 02:41.920
Come on.

02:54.520 --> 02:56.240
It's all right, ma'am. It's all right.

02:56.320 --> 03:00.720
Come inside. Come inside.
Stay inside, don't come out.

03:24.360 --> 03:26.360
[gunfire]

04:09.960 --> 04:13.560
Get away from the window.
Right, stay inside and stay down.

04:22.600 --> 04:24.920
[baby crying]

04:26.040 --> 04:29.360
Everyone stay indoors! Stay down!

04:29.480 --> 04:31.720
-By order of the Peaky Blinders.
-Come on!

04:43.800 --> 04:45.800
[baby continues crying]

05:06.880 --> 05:07.760
[snaps fingers]

05:24.360 --> 05:25.320
Come here.

05:32.480 --> 05:34.320
[breathing shakily]

05:34.400 --> 05:37.200
Which way?
Which way did he go?

05:40.920 --> 05:43.920
You sure? Yeah?

05:59.760 --> 06:01.480
[panting]

06:11.320 --> 06:13.400
[indistinct voices approaching]

06:34.560 --> 06:36.840
-[gunfire]
-[man grunts]

06:36.920 --> 06:38.000
Oy! [in Italian]

06:38.120 --> 06:39.240
It's me!

06:45.800 --> 06:47.800
[panting]

07:13.080 --> 07:13.920
Oy!

07:15.240 --> 07:16.160
[screams]

07:20.240 --> 07:21.120
Luca.

07:21.240 --> 07:22.400
[in Italian]
Let's get out of here.

07:22.480 --> 07:23.320
No.

07:23.640 --> 07:26.440
He knows these streets. We don't.

07:27.360 --> 07:30.240
We have him cornered. We've got him.

07:34.560 --> 07:36.600
[groaning]

07:43.040 --> 07:44.240
[in Italian]

07:44.360 --> 07:45.560
Fucking animal, to shoot a wounded man.

07:46.520 --> 07:47.720
You will be avenged.

08:02.320 --> 08:06.240
What are you trying to do?
Get yourself killed?

08:08.520 --> 08:13.520
[in English] Hey! I know you own the cops
in this dirty fucking town.

08:14.360 --> 08:16.760
But you'll dead before they get here.

08:18.240 --> 08:19.880
Come on, me and you, Tommy.

08:22.360 --> 08:23.200
Come on.

08:36.159 --> 08:37.400
[in Italian]

08:37.480 --> 08:38.919
Dear Lord.

08:40.799 --> 08:43.120
Vengeance is yours.

08:44.640 --> 08:48.800
My Father. Look upon me.

08:50.240 --> 08:51.880
Vengeance...

08:54.200 --> 08:55.800
...is yours too.

09:03.120 --> 09:04.640
-[gunshot]
-[men clamoring]

09:04.720 --> 09:06.040
[policeman] Stop what you're doing!

09:06.160 --> 09:08.120
[overlapping shouting]

09:15.280 --> 09:17.160
Go back, mate, you moron!

09:17.680 --> 09:18.720
[grunts]

09:25.840 --> 09:26.680
Enough!

09:26.800 --> 09:29.960
I said enough! I said enough!

09:30.040 --> 09:33.200
No. Now, get out of it. Get away!

09:34.160 --> 09:35.000
Enough.

09:35.080 --> 09:36.360
What the fuck are you doing here?

09:37.400 --> 09:40.000
Saving your life. Or his.

09:40.560 --> 09:42.080
I am a police officer, Tommy.

09:42.240 --> 09:47.800
I am a fucking police officer, right,
doing my duty. Stopping all this!

09:51.680 --> 09:54.160
There are three bodies need cleaning up.

09:54.760 --> 09:56.360
No. Enough.

09:56.840 --> 09:59.640
Tell the people who live in these houses

09:59.760 --> 10:03.560
that they are free
to go about their lawful business.

10:03.840 --> 10:07.800
Tell them that the rule of law
has been restored.

10:09.040 --> 10:11.480
Haven't you heard, Tommy, eh?

10:11.880 --> 10:13.360
Soldiers are coming.

10:34.840 --> 10:36.160
[pouring drink]

10:47.680 --> 10:50.440
[Polly] Do you know, I remember the very
first time you head-butted a policeman.

10:52.120 --> 10:55.440
But after you got your OBE from the King,
I didn't think there would be a next time.

11:04.360 --> 11:05.880
What do you think
you're going to tell Arthur?

11:08.200 --> 11:09.440
I will tell them the truth.

11:09.560 --> 11:10.520
[clears throat]

11:14.160 --> 11:15.000
[Polly] They are here.

11:35.280 --> 11:36.120
[Arthur] So...

11:38.880 --> 11:41.360
what the fuck happened today, Tom?

11:42.360 --> 11:45.280
We all heard.
Shooting in Artillery Square.

11:45.360 --> 11:46.640
Yeah, there was.

11:48.040 --> 11:49.400
Today I killed three men.

11:51.480 --> 11:53.000
Now our enemies will have to wait.

11:56.280 --> 11:57.760
I suppose they, uh...

11:58.800 --> 12:00.760
I suppose they took
you by surprise, did they?

12:00.840 --> 12:02.360
No. I knew they were coming.

12:05.240 --> 12:07.320
Just after Christmas I received a letter

12:08.400 --> 12:12.360
from Luca Changretta,
offering to spare my son

12:12.480 --> 12:13.760
if I gave up Tommy.

12:15.200 --> 12:16.360
And I gave Tommy up.

12:16.560 --> 12:19.000
Because that was the plan
that Polly and I agreed on.

12:19.920 --> 12:22.400
I knew that Luca would want
to pull the trigger himself...

12:22.760 --> 12:23.640
[sniffs]

12:23.720 --> 12:25.680
So I used the set up
as bait to bring him in.

12:27.080 --> 12:28.600
You are a fucking idiot, Tom.

12:29.240 --> 12:32.320
Look, I didn't get Luca,
but I got three. All right?

12:32.480 --> 12:34.160
That's it. That's what happened.

12:35.400 --> 12:37.720
-Come here, you.
-[man] Aye, but he's right, huh?

12:37.920 --> 12:39.520
I mean I thought you'd gone soft.

12:39.600 --> 12:40.760
[chuckles]

12:41.040 --> 12:42.880
-So, you got three?
-Yeah, I got three.

12:43.920 --> 12:46.240
Well, I drink to you, Tom,
you mad bastard.

12:46.600 --> 12:48.000
[all laugh]

12:55.360 --> 12:58.080
Pretty soon you are gonna get the shakes

12:58.200 --> 12:59.400
when your blood cools down.

13:00.280 --> 13:01.560
Let's go get a drink.

13:01.880 --> 13:03.960
Dad, you got three what?

13:05.120 --> 13:07.640
I got three shillings
for a two-shilling horse.

13:07.800 --> 13:10.040
Now, my boy, you come with us, huh?

13:34.360 --> 13:36.320
[door opens]

13:39.320 --> 13:40.400
Want a drink, Lizzie?

13:41.880 --> 13:42.960
I've had a hard day.

13:44.920 --> 13:47.040
I don't drink whiskey or gin anymore, Tom.

13:47.880 --> 13:48.720
Why not?

13:51.360 --> 13:52.880
Because they say it harms the baby.

14:00.200 --> 14:02.440
Yes. It can only be yours.

14:03.360 --> 14:06.000
That day by the canal when you were
fucking somebody else in your head,

14:07.760 --> 14:09.480
except it wasn't her who got pregnant.

14:16.720 --> 14:17.920
Have a seat, Lizzie.

14:31.000 --> 14:32.080
[sighs]

14:32.640 --> 14:33.960
All right, I know a woman, Lizzie.

14:34.040 --> 14:35.440
You know lots of women, Tommy.

14:36.920 --> 14:38.920
If you don't know this already
you don't know me.

14:40.040 --> 14:41.040
I am keeping it.

14:43.560 --> 14:45.160
Who's gonna run me fucking office?

14:48.760 --> 14:49.880
You will find somebody.

14:52.080 --> 14:52.920
Well...

14:55.320 --> 14:57.400
you better put a fucking advert
in the paper then.

14:57.800 --> 14:59.040
I'm not laid up yet.

15:00.680 --> 15:02.800
You'll not go to work
with a child of mine inside of you.

15:07.200 --> 15:08.800
Fuck, now me hand shakes.

15:11.720 --> 15:12.760
It's okay, Tom.

15:14.160 --> 15:15.080
It'll be okay.

15:18.400 --> 15:19.800
All this death, Lizzie.

15:21.520 --> 15:23.400
Fuck, let's have some life, right?

15:30.920 --> 15:32.360
I got three. [clears throat]

15:34.120 --> 15:34.960
I know, Tom.

15:37.000 --> 15:38.360
[sighs]

15:38.840 --> 15:40.160
One of them point-blank.

15:41.920 --> 15:44.480
A baby. A little you and me.

15:48.400 --> 15:49.560
Point blank, Lizzie.

15:53.000 --> 15:54.280
And he looked up at me.

16:01.200 --> 16:02.280
[clears throat]

16:03.200 --> 16:04.160
[glass thuds]

16:07.040 --> 16:08.240
You will get an allowance

16:09.480 --> 16:11.160
every week from the company.

16:12.000 --> 16:13.160
Business is booming.

16:13.720 --> 16:15.920
I will buy you a nice house, eh?

16:19.000 --> 16:20.320
Come on, I will drive you home.

17:00.640 --> 17:02.000
I'm just looking.

17:06.359 --> 17:07.480
[glass shatters]

17:23.079 --> 17:24.760
[snorts]

17:31.280 --> 17:33.400
[cap twisting]

17:40.600 --> 17:41.440
Hmm?

17:51.480 --> 17:52.840
[door shuts]

17:56.000 --> 17:57.560
[footsteps approaching]

18:00.400 --> 18:01.640
-Fuck.
-Linda.

18:01.760 --> 18:03.040
Arthur, you scared me to death.

18:03.120 --> 18:04.080
Linda.

18:05.720 --> 18:06.760
[groans]

18:08.720 --> 18:11.920
Linda, I need you to save me. Again.

18:12.200 --> 18:13.880
You are drunk. Again.

18:14.280 --> 18:19.280
I'm drunk again. I am drunk again.

18:21.640 --> 18:23.400
I need you to save me.

18:25.480 --> 18:27.920
Tell me what you said to me this morning.

18:28.640 --> 18:31.840
[stutters] Tell me again. Tell me.

18:32.960 --> 18:35.480
Say it, say it, say it. Tell me.

18:36.720 --> 18:38.920
We'll be back in our garden

18:40.240 --> 18:43.320
before the time comes
to plant anything out.

18:44.920 --> 18:46.200
Just one winter.

18:47.920 --> 18:49.520
Just one winter.

18:56.320 --> 18:57.520
Come to bed, Arthur.

19:02.560 --> 19:03.400
[grunting]

19:04.560 --> 19:05.600
They're coming, boys.

19:33.440 --> 19:34.280
No.

19:36.480 --> 19:37.520
No fucking way.

19:38.000 --> 19:39.800
Have you ever eaten hedgehog, Michael?

19:39.880 --> 19:40.960
[laughter]

19:41.560 --> 19:42.800
I'm getting back in this car.

19:43.160 --> 19:46.600
Michael, you are number two
on Luca Changretta's hit list.

19:46.760 --> 19:48.240
Yeah, and I will stay in a hotel.

19:48.600 --> 19:49.760
You stay in a hotel,

19:50.280 --> 19:51.400
I'll know where you are,

19:51.560 --> 19:53.080
so will the people who take you there,

19:53.160 --> 19:54.840
so will the people who work in the hotel.

19:55.400 --> 19:57.240
And hotels don't move around.

19:58.480 --> 20:00.280
They don't even know
where they will be tomorrow.

20:00.800 --> 20:02.440
They follow the patrin and the crows.

20:02.880 --> 20:04.560
And if anyone should come
for you, Michael,

20:05.640 --> 20:08.240
the Palmers and the Boswells
will put up a fair fight.

20:11.360 --> 20:12.360
[Polly] Take your medicine.

20:14.280 --> 20:15.120
I'll take them.

20:15.280 --> 20:16.320
Your painkillers.

20:17.200 --> 20:19.960
But the healers up there
will heal you much quicker.

20:21.400 --> 20:23.120
Fucking witches, the lot of them.

20:23.640 --> 20:25.480
Show some respect, Mr. Gray.

20:26.440 --> 20:28.600
They've agreed to welcome you
on account of your blood.

20:35.920 --> 20:36.920
Take your medicine.

20:38.440 --> 20:39.400
Take the gun.

20:40.920 --> 20:42.320
I won't be able to contact you.

20:43.120 --> 20:44.160
Till you phone me.

20:46.080 --> 20:47.160
We'll make a plan.

20:50.680 --> 20:52.040
Tommy says it won't be long.

20:54.040 --> 20:55.080
Then we'll be free.

21:03.720 --> 21:05.400
You might learn something.

21:08.080 --> 21:11.640
Tell them your grandmother
was a gypsy princess.

21:12.200 --> 21:14.000
Name of Birdy Boswell.

21:14.960 --> 21:17.080
You're royalty up there, Michael.

21:20.000 --> 21:21.520
[horses neighing]

21:31.640 --> 21:32.880
[Aberama] Is that true, Mrs. Gray?

21:34.600 --> 21:35.440
What?

21:36.760 --> 21:38.240
Don't I look like royalty?

21:38.440 --> 21:40.480
Well, now that you've mentioned it,
you do.

21:47.840 --> 21:50.160
I've been cooped up
in Small Heath too long.

21:53.240 --> 21:55.120
I can smell spring in the air.

22:00.640 --> 22:02.360
Do you know a longer way back, Mr. Gold?

22:05.960 --> 22:08.720
I know ways back that would take forever.

22:09.840 --> 22:10.880
Get in, your majesty.

22:38.120 --> 22:39.440
I thought you were a busy woman.

22:43.080 --> 22:44.160
Do you have time for this?

22:44.800 --> 22:46.800
-Is it a buck?
-It is a buck.

22:48.320 --> 22:51.080
Good. Bucks taste better.

23:00.480 --> 23:02.600
In the smoke, I'm 16 again.

23:06.400 --> 23:08.960
You know, when the police were after him,
my dad used to take us out.

23:09.480 --> 23:11.520
We'd be gone for days
living on what he caught.

23:14.240 --> 23:15.080
Oh!

23:16.000 --> 23:17.080
Do you have a sharp knife?

23:29.120 --> 23:30.720
I heard you have second sight.

23:33.840 --> 23:35.600
I heard that you speak with the dead.

23:38.120 --> 23:38.960
Yes.

23:44.240 --> 23:47.720
Your wife is often around you.
She watches you.

23:50.480 --> 23:51.640
She watching me now?

23:59.240 --> 24:00.080
No.

24:04.720 --> 24:06.040
Your family were healers?

24:07.040 --> 24:08.280
Yeah, a long time ago.

24:12.040 --> 24:14.040
Came back when I put my head
in the noose.

24:17.480 --> 24:20.480
It's like putting your head through
a window and seeing the whole world.

24:24.120 --> 24:28.280
Give me the rabbit and the knife.

24:33.520 --> 24:34.480
You know, Polly...

24:36.760 --> 24:41.600
I believe it's you that has kept
Tommy Shelby alive all these years.

24:42.200 --> 24:43.800
Oh, we've kept each other alive.

24:47.120 --> 24:49.320
But I didn't just put my head
through that window.

24:51.680 --> 24:53.160
I climbed through it.

24:55.160 --> 24:57.800
At first, I thought it was madness but no,

24:59.280 --> 25:01.200
when you put your head
out of that window...

25:02.800 --> 25:05.360
you can do anything you want.

25:07.320 --> 25:08.960
'Cause there are no rules.

25:11.920 --> 25:13.560
'Cause there are no risks.

25:19.440 --> 25:20.960
Now, give me the knife.

25:39.120 --> 25:40.080
Now, come here.

25:46.480 --> 25:48.120
I can do whatever I want

25:49.640 --> 25:51.160
whenever the mood takes me

25:53.160 --> 25:55.120
and you're a strong handsome man

25:57.000 --> 25:59.320
and this is a beautiful place
in the world.

26:01.280 --> 26:04.840
And it is... this time.

26:19.200 --> 26:21.280
But let me make
one thing clear, Mr. Gold,

26:22.120 --> 26:23.760
I just gave Michael a little speech

26:23.840 --> 26:25.840
about how no one
would know where to find him.

26:27.320 --> 26:28.640
But you would know how to get him.

26:30.000 --> 26:31.600
If any harm comes to Michael,

26:32.400 --> 26:34.160
you shall have me as your enemy

26:35.680 --> 26:38.320
and none of your knives can kill me.

26:41.840 --> 26:42.880
Do you understand?

26:43.920 --> 26:45.160
Oh, I understand.

26:48.400 --> 26:50.120
[in Romani]
A beautiful ghost you are

26:52.240 --> 26:53.080
...and free.

27:46.000 --> 27:47.120
Mr. Solomons.

27:47.800 --> 27:48.760
Hmm?

27:50.800 --> 27:52.720
My little cousin was born blind.

27:54.000 --> 27:55.040
As a result,

27:55.200 --> 27:58.960
I now donate a considerable
sum of money to a charity

27:59.040 --> 28:03.080
which gives dogs with eyes to blind Jews.

28:05.000 --> 28:06.720
The chairman of the board

28:06.800 --> 28:11.600
recommends that those of us
who are blessed with the gift of sight

28:11.680 --> 28:17.160
and that we spend at least half an hour
of our day with our eyes closed

28:17.280 --> 28:20.640
so that we may...
We may have a better understanding

28:21.880 --> 28:27.800
with the darkness and also
to increase our donations and that.

28:27.880 --> 28:28.840
Hmm.

28:30.480 --> 28:31.480
What time is it?

28:35.320 --> 28:36.960
Twenty-nine minutes past eight.

28:37.040 --> 28:41.440
Right, well then, I have another minute
to go actually but you...

28:43.320 --> 28:44.760
you can begin, go on.

28:44.920 --> 28:45.960
[smacks lips]

28:56.120 --> 28:58.000
I'm Luca Changretta.

28:58.520 --> 29:00.320
Oh, yeah, I know who you are. Hmm.

29:00.680 --> 29:02.720
You are a bit of a failure, aren't you?

29:02.920 --> 29:05.880
You come all the way over here
to this country

29:05.960 --> 29:10.280
in order to kill Tommy Shelby,
but I mean...

29:11.600 --> 29:13.440
Well, he is not dead, is he? So...

29:13.560 --> 29:15.080
-No.
-No.

29:15.600 --> 29:16.440
He ain't.

29:17.400 --> 29:19.640
How much time have I got left, mate?

29:22.440 --> 29:26.520
Ten seconds. Nine seconds, eight seconds,

29:27.800 --> 29:31.720
five, four, three,

29:32.800 --> 29:34.880
two, one.

29:37.040 --> 29:38.240
Right. Hello.

29:40.640 --> 29:42.040
How can I help you?

29:45.760 --> 29:47.280
I have a proposition for you.

29:47.360 --> 29:51.280
Mmm... Yeah. I already know what you want.

29:51.600 --> 29:54.560
-Yeah.
-I just want to hear you say it out loud.

29:54.800 --> 29:57.960
So I can check how ridiculous it is.

29:58.360 --> 29:59.240
[in Italian]

29:59.320 --> 30:01.320
Ok, I have my own 10 seconds of patience
left with this guy.

30:01.400 --> 30:02.240
[Matteo] Luca.

30:02.360 --> 30:03.280
-[grunts]
-[in Italian]

30:03.360 --> 30:08.200
They say this is how he is. We need him.

30:12.080 --> 30:15.400
[in English] There is gonna be
a little fight, a boxing match.

30:15.760 --> 30:18.240
Between your boy and Tommy Shelby's boy.

30:18.960 --> 30:21.240
-Right, Birmingham?
-Mmm-hmm.

30:21.320 --> 30:23.800
And the whole Shelby family
is gonna be there.

30:23.880 --> 30:24.760
Mmm-hmm.

30:25.760 --> 30:30.360
And you, Mr. Solomons,
you too will be there.

30:31.640 --> 30:32.960
[stutters]

30:33.040 --> 30:33.880
That's it.

30:34.240 --> 30:35.840
I tell you what, right.

30:36.360 --> 30:38.760
Here is a gift. It's free.

30:38.880 --> 30:41.040
Souvenir of your visit here.

30:41.160 --> 30:44.760
Goodbye, trot on.
Down there is Bonnie Street.

30:52.440 --> 30:54.560
You know they say you're a smart guy.

30:54.920 --> 30:56.040
[chuckles]

30:56.320 --> 30:58.880
You already know
what we want before we say it.

31:00.800 --> 31:02.880
That's funny 'cause now I believe

31:03.400 --> 31:09.160
I know what you want
even before you say it. Yeah.

31:09.520 --> 31:10.600
So, are you gonna taste it?

31:20.480 --> 31:21.880
[in Italian]

31:22.000 --> 31:26.360
I think this clown wants us to
run his rum

31:27.520 --> 31:28.560
...into New York.

31:28.720 --> 31:29.960
Damn fucking straight, mate.

31:30.040 --> 31:32.920
Otherwise, you wouldn't still be breathing
my oxygen, would you?

31:33.040 --> 31:35.400
Because I have 200 barrels a month.

31:35.480 --> 31:39.400
Yeah, cleared by your people,
distributed through your teams...

31:39.480 --> 31:42.920
Thing is that people want gin these days.

31:44.160 --> 31:49.120
Well, the exit is still out there.
Right on Bonnie Street. Yeah?

31:50.720 --> 31:51.840
[Luca chuckles]

31:51.920 --> 31:54.200
[Luca] Oh,
you fucking crazy, you know that?

31:55.360 --> 31:57.560
Two hundred barrels, huh?

32:00.000 --> 32:01.040
