33:18.720 --> 33:22.880
I have people that I trust, okay?
So you are gonna take my boys

33:23.440 --> 33:25.880
and you are gonna bring them
to the ring as seconds.

33:27.000 --> 33:29.120
Well, in order to qualify
as my seconds, right,

33:29.200 --> 33:32.280
they would first have to qualify
as being Jewish. Yeah?

33:33.120 --> 33:35.120
And in order to do that
they would have to replace

33:35.200 --> 33:37.760
their natural Italian fucking arrogance

33:37.840 --> 33:41.520
with a Jewish air of absolute certainty.

33:42.200 --> 33:45.040
You see, my good friend, Tommy Shelby,
he will know the difference.

33:46.320 --> 33:49.920
These days, back in the old country,

33:51.480 --> 33:53.920
a lot of the...
You know, the Jewish people,

33:54.000 --> 34:00.400
they... [chuckles] are having to pass
themselves off as Italian.

34:00.560 --> 34:02.000
[laughing]

34:02.080 --> 34:05.640
All right, well, you'll have to add
another ton onto your bill

34:06.280 --> 34:07.880
for being a cunt, mate.

34:09.159 --> 34:10.000
All right?

34:13.320 --> 34:14.320
[snaps fingers]

34:15.199 --> 34:19.520
You will bring my men to Birmingham?

34:21.880 --> 34:23.520
You will circumcise them?

34:25.080 --> 34:27.199
Yeah, you will have to circumcise them.

34:27.880 --> 34:30.400
Because the peakys will check, yeah?

34:31.639 --> 34:32.480
[in Italian]

34:32.560 --> 34:34.000
Piece of shit.

34:35.480 --> 34:39.159
Okay, any other requests?

34:39.480 --> 34:42.800
Two hundred fucking barrels,
we have a deal.

34:44.600 --> 34:45.600
Uh...

34:46.800 --> 34:48.040
[exhales]

34:48.120 --> 34:50.360
-What's the matter?
-Mmm. Well...

34:51.080 --> 34:52.360
I said we have a deal.

34:53.040 --> 34:56.480
Eh, you just made a deal
without a negotiation, didn't you?

34:58.520 --> 34:59.360
Huh.

35:00.200 --> 35:02.680
Yeah, Tommy Shelby
was right about you, wasn't he?

35:05.560 --> 35:06.560
[in Yiddish]

35:06.640 --> 35:09.160
You plan to kill us all.

35:10.080 --> 35:11.040
[clicks tongue]

35:34.200 --> 35:36.880
-[officer] Ada Shelby?
-No.

35:49.320 --> 35:50.400
[keys jangling]

35:50.560 --> 35:51.400
[door opens]

36:01.040 --> 36:03.680
She was armed when we picked her up, sir.
So we strip searched her.

36:03.760 --> 36:05.280
-That will be all.
-Yes, sir.

36:06.120 --> 36:08.040
[Colonel Ben Younger]
I apologize, Miss Shelby.

36:09.840 --> 36:12.440
-The territorials can be over-zealous.
-[door opens and shuts]

36:13.320 --> 36:14.600
Your men watched.

36:14.760 --> 36:16.120
And they will be reprimanded.

36:16.440 --> 36:17.880
They won't see Saturday.

36:19.400 --> 36:23.160
A naked woman alone making threats
against the entire British Army.

36:24.280 --> 36:26.200
Significant indicator of character.

36:30.160 --> 36:33.120
I'll turn my back while you dress
and perhaps we can talk.

36:36.120 --> 36:38.920
I have a dossier
on each member of your family.

36:39.760 --> 36:42.080
I know your family's
extraordinary history.

36:42.160 --> 36:43.520
[chuckles] Fuck you.

36:43.880 --> 36:45.320
And I also have a totally blank page

36:45.400 --> 36:48.120
on which together we can write
your family's immediate future.

36:49.560 --> 36:51.040
You rehearsed your speech.

36:51.440 --> 36:54.120
Significant indicator
of a lack of confidence.

36:54.280 --> 36:55.760
-What rank are you?
-Colonel.

36:56.240 --> 36:57.560
-Well...
-May I turn?

36:57.640 --> 36:59.560
Not unless you want to get blinded.

37:00.200 --> 37:02.800
I'm sorry this has got off to a bad start.

37:04.000 --> 37:05.080
What is this?

37:05.400 --> 37:08.960
Three days ago, you were seen at a meeting
for the Stetford Communist Party.

37:09.280 --> 37:12.000
You were then seen talking
to a woman called Jessie Eden.

37:13.320 --> 37:14.280
Turn around.

37:20.920 --> 37:21.760
I'm leaving.

37:24.680 --> 37:27.400
And you can burn this.
It's history.

37:30.520 --> 37:31.520
Ada Shelby,

37:32.400 --> 37:35.840
a person of interest and under
the surveillance of the special branch

37:36.000 --> 37:38.200
since you joined
the Birmingham Communist Party

37:38.280 --> 37:39.960
in June 1919.

37:41.240 --> 37:43.520
I'm no longer a member
of the Communist Party.

37:43.760 --> 37:45.920
I know. Irrelevant.

37:46.840 --> 37:48.720
Most of the more active subversives

37:48.800 --> 37:51.160
shed their official allegiances
to avoid detection.

37:51.560 --> 37:55.080
[scoffs] Look... okay.
Let me explain it to you.

37:55.160 --> 37:57.720
I'm no longer a member
of the Communist Party

37:58.000 --> 38:00.680
because I'm no longer a believer
in the cause of socialism.

38:00.760 --> 38:02.120
Now, open that door.

38:02.520 --> 38:06.240
[Colonel Ben Younger] So, in the past,
you were blinded by love?

38:08.280 --> 38:10.880
No. Blinded by faith.

38:11.600 --> 38:13.760
I believed people deserved justice.

38:14.640 --> 38:15.480
They don't.

38:16.360 --> 38:20.120
So, you've arrested me
because I had a drink with Jessie Eden?

38:20.680 --> 38:24.400
Whiskey with ice for you
and a beer for her.

38:28.080 --> 38:31.160
I met Jessie Eden
to settle an industrial dispute.

38:32.200 --> 38:33.240
Head of acquisitions?

38:34.000 --> 38:35.120
So, you swapped sides.

38:35.360 --> 38:37.680
If you know what I drink,
you know what I do for a living.

38:39.040 --> 38:39.920
Miss Shelby,

38:41.600 --> 38:44.680
you must understand
that these are extraordinary times.

38:45.120 --> 38:46.360
A general strike is certain.

38:46.720 --> 38:48.240
Attempted revolution perhaps.

38:49.040 --> 38:51.800
Soldiers on the streets very soon.
They are already drilling.

38:53.120 --> 38:54.560
And here stands you.

38:56.040 --> 38:58.360
A woman with her foot in both camps.

38:59.200 --> 39:00.480
It's potentially very useful.

39:02.320 --> 39:03.400
Useful to who?

39:05.120 --> 39:06.960
Maybe you should ask your brother, Thomas.

39:14.520 --> 39:15.720
[door opens]

39:23.000 --> 39:27.280
[man] Put some fucking effort into it,
the fight's in two days.

39:28.280 --> 39:29.880
Get used to the reach.

39:31.800 --> 39:33.640
Get used to the long arm on him.

39:35.480 --> 39:36.800
Get under it.

39:39.800 --> 39:41.520
That's it, under his body, boy.

39:53.320 --> 39:55.520
Talk to me about Colonel Ben Younger.

40:00.080 --> 40:00.920
What about him?

40:01.720 --> 40:03.320
He has just made me a proposition.

40:07.400 --> 40:08.400
You're in my chair.

40:10.600 --> 40:12.120
He said you knew about it.

40:12.200 --> 40:13.160
[pours drink]

40:13.240 --> 40:14.880
And remember
I know when you are lying.

40:16.480 --> 40:21.600
Ben Younger was an officer
in the Warwickshire Yeomanry in Flanders.

40:24.400 --> 40:27.120
The only cavalryman
who could ride a fucking horse.

40:27.480 --> 40:29.080
I was strip searched.

40:32.280 --> 40:33.920
Two soldiers watched.

40:36.000 --> 40:37.880
I am sorry, Ada.

40:39.880 --> 40:40.760
That...

40:42.920 --> 40:45.960
The arrest was so the neighbors
would see and word would go around.

40:46.960 --> 40:48.360
Younger is all right.

40:52.600 --> 40:54.360
Younger came to me for help.

40:56.360 --> 40:57.320
[groans]

40:58.520 --> 40:59.880
He has been given Birmingham.

41:00.280 --> 41:02.160
Given Birmingham. By who?

41:03.320 --> 41:06.240
By Churchill.
By the fucking King.

41:07.560 --> 41:09.320
By people who want to stop a revolution.

41:09.400 --> 41:10.280
[scoffs]

41:10.920 --> 41:12.640
No one is laughing anymore, Ada.

41:14.920 --> 41:17.040
The home office is making provisions.

41:17.960 --> 41:19.800
This is part of those provisions.

41:21.160 --> 41:25.240
And how is Tommy Shelby, OBE,
going to stop a revolution?

41:26.640 --> 41:29.040
Jessie Eden has accepted
my invitation to dinner.

41:29.120 --> 41:30.080
[scoffs]

41:30.160 --> 41:31.440
Of course. I'm sorry.

41:31.760 --> 41:34.920
Tommy Shelby is gonna stop
the revolution with his cock.

41:37.040 --> 41:39.040
It's not her the military
are interested in,

41:39.120 --> 41:40.320
it's the people around her.

41:42.160 --> 41:45.320
The people like you used to be,
like Freddy used to be.

41:46.200 --> 41:47.760
People who want an armed revolution.

41:50.600 --> 41:52.160
If I get Jessie Eden's trust,

41:53.240 --> 41:55.320
she gives me the names of the instigators,

41:56.640 --> 41:58.320
I give them up to the crown forces.

41:59.080 --> 42:01.480
Tommy, Tommy, sweetheart.

42:02.560 --> 42:06.040
Why would a man whose medals rust
at the bottom of the Saltley canal

42:06.120 --> 42:07.880
want to help the British military?

42:11.840 --> 42:12.800
[sighs]

42:12.880 --> 42:17.200
Because I have been offered
three five-year contracts

42:18.760 --> 42:22.640
to supply military vehicles
to the British forces in India,

42:22.720 --> 42:28.160
Ceylon, Singapore and Burma.
Total value £2 million.

42:31.640 --> 42:34.840
Wouldn't be no strikes in your factory
'cause Jessie Eden would be in your bed.

42:39.040 --> 42:41.520
Tommy, this can only happen
if you are still alive.

42:41.920 --> 42:43.120
Planning on staying alive.

42:44.440 --> 42:48.040
If I'm dead you can all go back
to being what you were.

42:51.200 --> 42:54.000
The British army came to me, Ada.

42:57.360 --> 42:58.440
I said, why not.

43:01.520 --> 43:03.200
I'll put that on your grave, Tom.

43:06.280 --> 43:09.360
Tommy Shelby, "Why not."

43:12.600 --> 43:13.840
[sighs]

43:14.080 --> 43:15.400
Are you gonna help me or not?

43:23.440 --> 43:24.400
[door shuts]

43:32.800 --> 43:34.200
[clattering]

43:37.480 --> 43:38.720
Other way around.

43:46.520 --> 43:49.000
And... will they want music, Charlie?

43:49.080 --> 43:52.760
We have that gramophone we found
abandoned inside that gentleman's car.

43:52.840 --> 43:55.880
No, they don't.
Tommy said they are here to talk.

43:56.640 --> 43:58.040
[door creaks open]

44:05.320 --> 44:07.680
Charlie, Curly, this is Jessie Eden.

44:09.120 --> 44:13.720
Jessie, this is my uncle, Charlie
and my whatever Curly is.

44:14.080 --> 44:15.040
This is actually lovely.

44:15.120 --> 44:17.440
We were just wondering
if you'd like some music?

44:17.520 --> 44:20.040
-No, we weren't.
-Actually, Jessie likes music.

44:20.200 --> 44:23.640
-Don't go to any trouble.
-No, Curly, go to some trouble.

44:24.800 --> 44:25.760
Go on, then.

44:33.440 --> 44:34.280
Right.

44:47.920 --> 44:49.200
[clears throat]

44:52.880 --> 44:54.040
Don't I get a choice?

44:54.120 --> 44:55.840
I want an opinion. Try it.

45:04.000 --> 45:05.160
I don't really drink gin.

45:05.720 --> 45:06.720
Then you're perfect.

45:06.800 --> 45:09.280
My gin is for women
that don't really drink gin.

45:09.720 --> 45:10.560
Your gin?

45:11.600 --> 45:13.960
Let's drink to something.
You choose.

45:16.920 --> 45:18.040
To the revolution.

45:20.080 --> 45:20.960
Why not?

45:23.000 --> 45:24.600
-To the revolution.
-To the revolution.

45:27.520 --> 45:30.400
Right, well, since I have invited you
for dinner I thought I'd cook.

45:31.800 --> 45:34.760
These two beauties were shot this morning

45:34.920 --> 45:38.680
by a poacher friend of mine
on Lord Packwood's estate.

45:39.480 --> 45:40.600
I thought you would like that.

45:41.040 --> 45:45.840
These here...
these were stolen from under his trees.

45:49.320 --> 45:52.520
Mr. Shelby, I came to talk business.

45:52.880 --> 45:53.720
Yes.

45:54.880 --> 45:55.800
So did I.

46:01.480 --> 46:02.920
Wage cuts withdrawn.

46:03.400 --> 46:05.560
Parity between men
and women guaranteed.

46:06.360 --> 46:08.520
You can instruct your members
to return to work tomorrow.

46:11.320 --> 46:14.520
And all I have to do in return is tell you
everything I know about socialism?

46:15.440 --> 46:16.760
That's what your sister said.

46:18.960 --> 46:20.040
You don't like your gin?

46:22.200 --> 46:23.040
It's okay.

46:25.040 --> 46:26.080
It's okay.

46:29.320 --> 46:30.920
What do you want to know about the cause?

46:34.760 --> 46:37.280
I'm approaching
the current political crisis

46:37.960 --> 46:40.320
as I would approach a horse race.

46:42.960 --> 46:44.760
Assessing the runners and the riders.

46:48.760 --> 46:51.680
Now, the favorite
is of course the King's horse.

46:53.880 --> 46:56.680
But the King's horse
was also the favorite in 1913,

46:57.240 --> 46:59.640
when Emily Davison
threw herself in front of it.

46:59.920 --> 47:01.360
You know the names of the suffragettes?

47:03.040 --> 47:04.000
I'm impressed.

47:04.280 --> 47:06.640
Oh, everyone laughed at them at first,
but now look.

47:07.760 --> 47:09.840
Women with serious faces everywhere.

47:13.240 --> 47:15.520
When I study a horse race,
I study form...

47:16.520 --> 47:20.360
and the other horse, the one
that wants to beat the King's horse.

47:22.960 --> 47:24.800
Let's call her Dangerous, shall we?

47:25.240 --> 47:26.320
She's has no form.

47:27.120 --> 47:28.520
That's what makes her so dangerous.

47:28.640 --> 47:31.360
Russia. Isn't that form?

47:31.560 --> 47:34.800
No. The Russians aren't like
the English with beer.

47:35.160 --> 47:36.160
They're petrol.

47:37.840 --> 47:39.400
That's why I invited you here for dinner.

47:41.480 --> 47:43.000
'Cause you know people,

47:44.680 --> 47:46.320
people that want to make this fight real.

47:46.760 --> 47:48.640
With guns and ammunition.

47:50.440 --> 47:52.720
So before I place a bet
on who is gonna win,

47:53.840 --> 47:55.240
I need to know how strong they are.

47:56.120 --> 47:57.280
How serious they are.

47:59.320 --> 48:02.200
Your concern
is that if the unthinkable happened,

48:03.600 --> 48:06.400
you would find yourself
on the wrong side of the barricades.

48:07.840 --> 48:09.040
Well, as you can see...

48:10.440 --> 48:14.640
my natural side of the barricades
is the same as yours and as you know...

48:16.720 --> 48:18.200
I once believed.

48:19.640 --> 48:20.920
But the war changed you?

48:23.800 --> 48:24.640
Yeah.

48:28.520 --> 48:32.600
The man I loved couldn't speak
when he got back. Not one word.

48:35.120 --> 48:37.240
I've said very few true words since.

48:40.120 --> 48:42.480
The men who blew the whistles
in France are our enemy.

48:44.960 --> 48:47.400
And you count yourself
among those who want a real fight?

48:48.280 --> 48:49.120
I do.

48:50.240 --> 48:51.640
-Well, well.
-Yes.

48:52.400 --> 48:54.400
Not just in my dreams, in the day now.

48:56.680 --> 48:57.680
And you're not alone.

48:58.920 --> 48:59.880
I'm not alone.

49:01.880 --> 49:02.720
Well, well.

49:05.720 --> 49:06.880
I have researched you.

49:08.920 --> 49:10.240
We have researched you.

49:12.560 --> 49:14.360
You've never been
a friend to the government.

49:15.040 --> 49:16.080
They've used you.

49:17.760 --> 49:19.440
And I imagine you have found out already

49:19.520 --> 49:22.400
that no amount of money allows you
to pass through the steel sheets

49:22.480 --> 49:24.360
-that separate class from class?
-[scoffs]

49:27.160 --> 49:31.600
Yes. Yes, that I have learnt.

49:33.320 --> 49:34.880
A man like you would terrify them.

49:36.240 --> 49:38.040
Man better than them at what they do.

49:38.560 --> 49:39.440
[chuckles]

49:40.840 --> 49:43.280
Would I change the odds, do you think?

49:45.320 --> 49:46.800
[footsteps approach]

49:47.720 --> 49:49.000
[Curly] It's all wound up, Tom.

49:49.080 --> 49:52.640
Uh, just put the needle on
and let her spin,

49:53.000 --> 49:56.040
and there are some
popular records, mostly romantic.

49:56.320 --> 49:57.200
Uh...

49:58.600 --> 49:59.640
Thank you, Curly.

50:06.840 --> 50:07.960
Dinner's nearly ready.

50:10.320 --> 50:12.080
Let's speak before we dance, shall we?

50:13.400 --> 50:14.400
So we are going to dance?

50:16.960 --> 50:17.800
I think so.

50:21.320 --> 50:22.360
[record snaps in]

50:24.560 --> 50:25.440
[clicks]

50:25.560 --> 50:27.360
[soft music plays]

50:27.680 --> 50:28.840
[Jessie chuckles]

50:28.920 --> 50:30.960
[Tommy] I swear to God.

50:31.080 --> 50:32.360
She gave me sixpence.

50:33.120 --> 50:37.280
She sends me to the shop
for margarine, eggs and bread.

50:37.560 --> 50:38.440
When I came back...

50:38.840 --> 50:40.240
...with a top hat and a coconut.

50:40.320 --> 50:42.920
...and that was all the money we had
for the whole fucking week.

50:43.920 --> 50:46.680
And me mum beat me
with a fucking frying pan.

50:47.000 --> 50:49.400
Why the hell did you buy
a top hat and a coconut?

50:49.480 --> 50:50.920
'Cause I thought she deserved it.

50:51.480 --> 50:52.640
I thought we all did.

50:53.120 --> 50:54.680
And I could never understand...

50:56.880 --> 51:00.720
why people like us
only had bread and fucking lard.

51:02.720 --> 51:04.400
And I wanted to be different.

51:05.400 --> 51:06.440
That's what I wanted.

51:09.480 --> 51:10.480
And you are?

51:12.760 --> 51:13.600
No.

51:16.000 --> 51:19.480
When I showed you that photo
of Greta Durruti, your face changed.

51:24.040 --> 51:25.840
She wanted everything to be different.

51:27.600 --> 51:29.080
Her whole world.

51:30.040 --> 51:30.880
As do I.

51:36.240 --> 51:37.440
Shall we hear some more music?

51:40.800 --> 51:41.680
[clears throat]

51:41.800 --> 51:43.200
[gramophone clicking]

51:44.760 --> 51:46.400
You were married but she was killed.

51:51.480 --> 51:53.840
"Bye, bye Blackbird"
reminds you of your sweetheart, eh?

51:55.200 --> 51:56.040
Yes.

51:58.000 --> 51:59.280
You want it fast or slow?

51:59.960 --> 52:03.000
Absolutely slow.
Would you just sit, I'm drunk.

52:03.280 --> 52:04.680
[record crackling]

52:08.720 --> 52:09.560
Come on.

52:11.920 --> 52:14.400
[music playing]

52:34.480 --> 52:35.640
Will you help us, Tommy?

53:15.440 --> 53:18.240
Soon. Soon.

53:23.360 --> 53:27.080
Arrange a meeting
with the appropriate people

53:28.200 --> 53:29.200
and I will be there.

53:36.400 --> 53:38.120
[crowd chattering]

53:38.200 --> 53:39.840
[sniffing]

53:41.120 --> 53:45.040
[Arthur] Billy, come on, boy.
Get over here, you lazy bastard.

53:46.080 --> 53:48.480
There, what's all that? Hey.

53:48.560 --> 53:49.840
[laughs]

53:51.080 --> 53:53.440
The room is clean, Mr. Shelby.

53:53.520 --> 53:56.080
Right. Lock it all down.

53:57.400 --> 53:59.160
All right, boys, lock it down.

54:07.200 --> 54:11.240
[man] No weapons!
No admission if you've any weapons!

54:15.880 --> 54:16.760
[grunts]

54:16.840 --> 54:17.720
Go on!

54:21.560 --> 54:25.120
Arthur! Can I open the book?

54:25.200 --> 54:27.600
All right. Open it up! You.

54:33.640 --> 54:34.640
Gentlemen.

54:35.760 --> 54:39.280
And in the cinema you blow your money
on the go. You hear me?

54:39.680 --> 54:41.920
It's fucking fight night. Clear the way.

54:46.040 --> 54:47.400
[man] Come on, boys.

54:47.480 --> 54:53.120
Come place your bets with me,
Honest Johnny Dodds.

54:53.200 --> 54:58.800
The only show in town in order
of your special constable brothers,

54:59.360 --> 55:01.240
the Peaky fucking Blinders.

55:16.120 --> 55:19.000
Bonnie, boy. Here we go, boy.

55:19.680 --> 55:22.440
Bring out that fucking tiger, eh. Go on.

55:22.920 --> 55:24.040
Tiger is already out.

55:24.640 --> 55:25.800
Fair enough.

55:27.080 --> 55:28.040
[Aberama] Bonnie...

55:28.520 --> 55:30.560
Mr. Shelby will give you a 20% cut

55:30.640 --> 55:32.720
if you put Goliath down
in the fourth round.

55:33.480 --> 55:35.160
[Arthur] Been caged up too long, brother.

55:37.880 --> 55:40.560
If the women are gonna have fun,
so am I.

55:59.680 --> 56:02.000
[chattering]

56:54.200 --> 56:56.440
♪ On the gathering storm comes ♪

56:56.520 --> 56:58.360
♪ A tall, handsome man ♪

56:58.440 --> 57:00.440
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

57:00.520 --> 57:02.560
♪ A red right hand ♪
